# Overleaf-compatible LaTeX image
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY NOT THE LITERAL OVERLEAF IMAGE?
# Overleaf's own compile images (quay.io/sharelatex/texlive-full) are NOT
# publicly pullable -- they are gated behind Overleaf Server Pro. Verified:
# `docker manifest inspect` returns "no such manifest" for their tags.
#
# So we use ghcr.io/ayaka-notes/texlive-full: a full TeX Live image built
# specifically to MIRROR Overleaf's environment (Overleaf CE/Pro). It IS
# publicly pullable (verified) and tagged by TeX Live year.
#
# >> CHOOSE THE RIGHT YEAR <<
# Match the tag to your Overleaf project's TeX Live version
# (Overleaf: Menu > Settings > TeX Live version). Tags: 2020.1 ... 2026.1.
# Reference: https://github.com/ayaka-notes/texlive-full
#
# Full TeX Live scheme, so abntex2, fontspec and babel-portuges are already
# included (no tlmgr install). Public pull (no docker login), multi-arch
# (amd64/arm64), large on first pull.
FROM ghcr.io/ayaka-notes/texlive-full:2024.1
